    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d51-a2">

                <pb facs="0148" n="66" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg66"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul to the
                            Commissioner for Foreign Affairs</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foochow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-04-03"><hi rendition="#italic">April 3,
                        1911</hi></date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2330.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your dispatch dated March 27, 1911, re the Chinese code of nationality, and
                    in reply would say that the law of the American Government prohibits the
                    naturalization of Chinese in the territory of the United States; and that I am
                    forwarding a copy of your dispatch to the American Legation at Peking. I will
                    communicate with your honor again on the subject, when I receive a reply from
                    the legation.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Samuel L. Gracey.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
